WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.112
Who is this for?

2
00:00:01.112 --> 00:00:06.020
Developers and identity engineers who
build the integrations behind joiners,

3
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.588
movers and leavers, and the
reviewers who approve each one.

4
00:00:09.588 --> 00:00:14.313
You'll want to read JSON and Python,
and you don't need a tenant until Lab 2.

5
00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:15.887
The roles are worth noticing.

6
00:00:15.887 --> 00:00:20.962
Creating an extension takes the Lifecycle
Workflows administrator role plus a

7
00:00:20.962 --> 00:00:26.037
contributor role on the Logic App's resource
group; the operator role isn't enough.

8
00:00:26.037 --> 00:00:29.595
The Logic App itself needs no
Graph permission to call back,

9
00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:33.650
and its downstream access should
be as narrow as the target allows.
